      "paragraphs": [
        "In 1969, R.H. Whittaker proposed the Five Kingdom Classification: Kingdom Monera, Kingdom Protista, Kingdom Fungi, Kingdom Plantae, and Kingdom Animalia.",
        "The criteria used for classification were: (1) Cell structure (prokaryotic vs eukaryotic), (2) Body / Thallus organisation (unicellular vs multicellular / tissue level), (3) Mode of nutrition (autotrophic vs heterotrophic, saprophytic vs holozoic), (4) Mode of reproduction, and (5) Phylogenetic (evolutionary) relationships.",
        "This solved key drawbacks of earlier systems: (a) Chlamydomonas and Spirogyra were earlier grouped under algae, but Chlamydomonas is unicellular while Spirogyra is multicellular. (b) Fungi (heterotrophic with chitinous cell walls) were placed under Plantae (autotrophic with cellulosic walls). (c) Unicellular protists were merged with plants or animals."
      ]
